{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally's Health and Lifestyle Column", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Meaning of Colors", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculating about Feelings and Impressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you speculate about something, you are making a guess based on what you know about the situation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can show you are speculating about something by using a modal, like <span class =\"italic\">must</span> or <span class =\"italic\">can't</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When the modal verb<span class =\"italic\"> must </span> is followed by <span class=\"italic\">have + a verb</span> in the past participle form, we are referring to a past action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The color green must have meant power in Egypt, but it is the color of youth in Japan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In Europe and North America, a \"yellow\" person is a coward, which can't be a good thing. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Someone's Feelings and Reactions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.<br/><br/>Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> are used to describe how a person feels, like <span class =\"italic\">excited, subdued, distressed, surprised, bored, worried</span> or <span class =\"italic\">tired</span>.<br/><br/>Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing</span> are used to describe things and situations, like <span class =\"italic\">exciting, subduing, distracting, distressing, boring, worrying</span> or <span class =\"italic\">tiring</span>. <br/>These adjectives describe the <span class =\"italic\">effect</span> something has on a person.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "People seem to get excited when exposed to red light and feel subdued when exposed to blue light. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Pink seems to be the most calming color of all.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "happiness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of being happy or content", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yellow was the color of happiness in ancient Egypt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about the meaning of colors.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "joy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling of great happiness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In China, the color red is the sign of happiness and joy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coward", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is constantly afraid", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In Europe and North America, a \"yellow\" person is a coward. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "calming", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes something that brings peace and calm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Pink seems to be the most calming color of all.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "jealousy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling that you envy what someone else has", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In North America, jealousy is called the \"green-eyed monster.\"", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "subdued", "type": "name"}, {"content": "calm; peaceful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  People seem to get excited when exposed to red light and feel subdued when exposed to blue light. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anger", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling of being angry or mad", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In Europe the color red means anger. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "power", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to decide things and make things happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The color green meant power in Egypt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose 5 colors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss what things each color may symbolize for you or for other people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the meanings you found for each color.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your list.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss cultures and traditions in relation to colors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read about the me