ontents": [{"content": "engenn7le02ob07re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}]}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "", "id": 1, "text": "All over the world, the colors red, yellow, and green on traffic lights have the same meaning: stop, caution, and go. In different countries, these colors may mean different things.", "time": "100"}, {"image": "", "id": 2, "text": "In China, the color red is the sign of happiness and joy, whereas in Europe it may mean anger. Yellow was the color of happiness in ancient Egypt, but in Europe and North America, a \"yellow\" person is a coward, which can't be a good thing. The color green must have meant power in Egypt, but it is the color of youth in Japan. A new worker or new immigrant is called \"green\" in some countries, but in North America jealousy is called the \"green-eyed monster.\"", "time": "13000"}, {"image": "", "id": 3, "text": "The different meaning of colors in different countries and cultures has developed over time. However, studies show that human beings everywhere react to certain colors in similar ways. For example, people seem to get excited when exposed to red light and feel subdued when exposed to blue light. Pink is closer to red than blue, but it seems to be the most calming color of all.", "time": "47000"}], "video_src": "engenn7le02ob07re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "video", "title": ""}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}]}